    input: objects may share rows across colors but not pixels; in every column, all top-color pixels must be above all bottom-color pixels (no path crossing)
    output: after sliding, same-color objects must not collide pixel-wise
    output_zones: top-zone and bottom-zone have >=5 empty bg rows between them
  swept_segment:
    applies only to bottom-color single-column objects where move distance < object height
    fills continuous column from original top row to final bottom row
    rare — only 1 instance across all examples
